import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
---
<Docs slug="browse">
  <p>
    The library is a grid of thumbnails, decoded as they scroll into view, so
    a folder of several thousand photos is browsable in seconds instead of
    loading everything up front. Everything below happens with the grid in
    front of you &mdash; you never have to open a photo to rate it.
  </p>

  <h2>Rate as you go</h2>
  <p>
    With a photo highlighted, press <kbd>0</kbd> to <kbd>5</kbd> to set the
    star rating, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>1</kbd> through
    <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>5</kbd> for a color label (red, yellow, green, blue,
    purple), and <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>0</kbd> to clear it. The Rating and
    Label tabs on the right do the same with the mouse.
  </p>

  <h2>Build a selection</h2>
  <p>
    Click to select, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+click to take a range,
    <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+click to toggle a single photo, and <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd>
    to take the whole folder. The arrow keys move the highlight;
    <kbd>Shift</kbd>+arrows extend the selection. A selection is what
    <a href="/docs/adjust.html">batch settings</a> and
    <a href="/docs/export.html">export</a> act on.
  </p>
</Docs>
